    // "Greens, mac & cheese & potato salad (green beans)". Two things say the
    // parenthetical is a VARIANT rather than a fourth dish. First, the corpus
    // uses it that way — repast's own dessert line elsewhere reads "...&
    // peach cobbler (red velvet)", which is plainly an alternative flavour, not
    // an extra cake. Second, the cost band below prices exactly three
    // components — collards, potatoes with eggs, and cheddar with pasta —
    // and never green beans. Counting green beans as a fourth dish would have
